      "writtenOn": "2024-12-17T17:57:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "General question, would it be possible to just use the feature in a lot of the `if` clauses in validation instead of needing both `Compat` + `HasFeature`? I\u0027m just imagining that in `Compat` by default the feature will be disabled, and in core it will be enabled by default? It just makes the conditions a little less cluttered.",
      "revId": "2c3c1dd90f7d4252979d1f5dab1d519ea3d0b721",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9cc21864_976b4f13",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-17T17:59:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess it boils down to whether this is a Compat specific feature versus just a feature in general?",
      "parentUuid": "9e5f0370_446c43fe",
      "revId": "2c3c1dd90f7d4252979d1f5dab1d519ea3d0b721",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ede43304_ab26c64a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-17T18:26:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Having the feature enabled by default in core would be a valid option. However, I think that would invalidate this WebGPU standard statement [1]\n```\nA device supports the exact set of features determined at creation.\n```\nSo when an user calls `APIGetFeatures`, it would return a list containing `FlexibleTextureViews` feature even though they never request for it.\n\nUnless we decide to make it a special feature such that it\u0027s only visible internally and won\u0027t be returned via `APIGetFeatures` in Core Mode. I think it makes the condition checks cleaner but the internal code would become more complicated due to having two sets of features.\n\n[1] https://www.w3.org/TR/webgpu/#features",
      "parentUuid": "9cc21864_976b4f13",
      "revId": "2c3c1dd90f7d4252979d1f5dab1d519ea3d0b721",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bd0db875_80796dac",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-17T18:28:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about adding a helper method in Device class instead. e.g.\n```\nbool HasFlexibleTextureViews() {\n\treturn !IsCompatMode() || HasFeature(FlexibleTextureViews);\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "ede43304_ab26c64a",
      "revId": "2c3c1dd90f7d4252979d1f5dab1d519ea3d0b721",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
