      "writtenOn": "2024-12-18T06:22:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e So when an user calls APIGetFeatures, it would return a list containing FlexibleTextureViews feature even though they never request for it.\n\nThe spec doesn\u0027t account for compat yet. This is in fact how we\u0027re intending to specify compat: all of these features that core has by default, but compat doesn\u0027t have, will get automatically enabled when creating a core device even if you didn\u0027t request them.\n\nSo I think it would be great to go ahead and make it behave like this (though the current code is not incorrect so it would be fine if this is a followup CL or a followup bug).",
      "parentUuid": "4693b872_ccd0fcb8",
      "revId": "2c3c1dd90f7d4252979d1f5dab1d519ea3d0b721",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
